        "attendance": 60338,
        "referee": "Chris Kavanagh",
        "standfirst": "Manchester City won 3-0 at Liverpool, scoring all three goals after Ryan Gravenberch was sent off.",
        "account": "Ryan Gravenberch received a second yellow card midway through the second half, leaving Liverpool with ten men at 0-0. Before it, in the 21st minute, Jérémy Jacquet had a shot from close range saved by Gianluigi Donnarumma. Erling Haaland scored three minutes after the red card, left-footed from inside the box and straight down the middle.\nJérémy Doku, on for Iliman Ndiaye, doubled the lead in the 68th minute, turning Elliot Anderson's pass into the top corner with his right foot from inside the area. Rayan Cherki made it 3-0 with 12 minutes left, the third goal in 13 minutes, finishing right-footed from inside the six-yard box after Josko Gvardiol, on for Nico O'Reilly, headed it to him.",
        "sections": [
          {
            "head": "Doku scores the second",
            "pitch": "Jérémy Doku came on from the bench with the match goalless and Liverpool still at full strength, and the goal he scored was the second of City's three.",
            "stake": "A free agent since domeitalycoach let him go on Wednesday; eight points."
          },
          {
            "head": "Cherki makes it four",
            "pitch": "Rayan Cherki had five shots, and the goal that completed the scoring was his fourth in the league this season.",
            "stake": "Cowthenbeef has him, for eight points."
          },
          {
            "head": "Haaland scores, Donnarumma saves",
            "pitch": "Erling Haaland's opener took him to six league goals for the season. Gianluigi Donnarumma made six saves and kept a clean sheet behind him.",
            "stake": "The Raccoons has Haaland, for six points; domeitalycoach has Donnarumma, for eight points."
          }
