        "standfirst": "Crystal Palace came from behind to beat Nottingham Forest 3-1.",
        "account": "Daichi Kamada levelled for Crystal Palace just before half-time, taking Quinten Timber's pass and sending a shot low into the corner. Dan Ndoye had put Nottingham Forest in front after three minutes with a low finish from within the area. Jefferson Lerma headed Adam Wharton's corner in from close range in first-half stoppage time, Palace scoring twice in eight minutes. Yéremy Pino struck low from inside the box after 59 minutes for 3-1.",
        "sections": [
          {
            "head": "Kamada brings Palace level",
            "pitch": "Daichi Kamada added a defensive point to the leveller, the goal that began Crystal Palace's recovery from an early deficit.",
            "stake": "His eight points are on the bench for The Truffle Pigs, more than the margin by which it trails Cowthenbeef 46-44; Cowthenbeef has one man to play, The Truffle Pigs none."
          },
          {
            "head": "Lerma busy both ends",
            "pitch": "Jefferson Lerma tried three shots in all, his headed goal among them, and earned two defensive points at the other end of the pitch.",
