        "standfirst": "Hull City drew 2-2 with Everton, Mohamed Belloumi levelling from the bench after Thierno Barry's goal.",
        "account": "Thierno Barry put Everton ahead after 68 minutes, striking Kiernan Dewsbury-Hall's pass into the top corner. Mohamed Belloumi, on for Joe Gelhardt, levelled with 16 minutes left, his finish from within the area going in high after a pass from Elliot Stroud, a substitute for Ryan Giles.\nBarry had a header from close range saved by Konstantinos Tzolakis after 27 minutes, from James Garner's cross. Brennan Johnson's goal for Everton was ruled out after a video review in the 34th minute. Joe Gelhardt opened the scoring just after half-time, meeting Sorba Thomas's through ball on the break and finishing low into the corner. Dewsbury-Hall headed Everton level after 55 minutes from Ainsley Maitland-Niles's corner, the ball going in low.",
